  "note": "Election of the whole Londonderry Corporation (North and South Wards two aldermen and six councillors each, Waterside one alderman and three councillors) under the Elections and Franchise Act (Northern Ireland) 1946; nominations closed Tuesday 1 October and the poll was on Wednesday 16 October 1946 (Returning Officer's notice of election, Derry Journal, 23 September 1946), results declared shortly after midnight. The councillorships in North and South were contested; the aldermen and the Waterside councillors had no poll. The Unionists kept the North Ward and so their 12 to 8 majority, while the six Derry Labour Party and Anti-Partition candidates took the South Ward (Derry Journal, 18 October 1946). Valid poll 4,768 (68 per cent). The six winners are marked with an asterisk in the Journal, footnoted 'Derry Labour Party and Anti-Partition'; that footnote is used as their label. Full names from the Returning Officer's notice."
